    "files": [
      {
        "path": "index.js",
        "content": "/*!\n * is-number <https://github.com/jonschlinkert/is-number>\n *\n * Copyright (c) 2014-2015, Jon Schlinkert.\n * Licensed under the MIT License.\n */\n\n'use strict';\n\nvar typeOf = require('kind-of');\n\nmodule.exports = function isNumber(num) {\n  var type = typeOf(num);\n  if (type !== 'number' && type !== 'string') {\n    return false;\n  }\n  if (type === 'string' && num.trim().length === 0) {\n    return false;\n  }\n  var n = +num;\n  return (n - n + 1) >= 0 && num !== '';\n};\n"
      }
    ],
    "requirements": "Independent maintainer issue #3 and original assertions: numeric values zero, one, and negative one, and numeric string \"1\" are numbers. Empty string, null, spaces-only string, and carriage-return/newline/tab-only string are not numbers. Preserve the public isNumber function and existing assertions. Make a source repair without changing any oracle or configuration.\n",
